## Runtime: part of the AIL native runtime; linked into user executables
## under the Runtime Exception (see LICENSE).
##
## Closure objects (type.fn.5, ADR 1067): word 0 is the code address of the
## function a call runs, words 1.. the values a function literal copied. The
## block is kind 13 (an environment record), which the collector scans word
## by word, so a copied pointer keeps its object alive.

FNLIT_KIND := 13

## A closure object of `n` words, zeroed; the caller fills them.
fn fnlit_new(n int) int
    alloc(8 * n, FNLIT_KIND)
